{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/201605-privilege-rewrites-to-core-changeling-entitlements","id":201605,"title":"Privilege rewrites to Core Changeling Entitlements","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-18T17:32:31-07:00","id":201605,"title":"Privilege rewrites to Core Changeling Entitlements","content":"I have been in several changeling larps and tabletops and I have noticed something rather unfortunate, almost no-one wants to play with an entitlement. The general concensus is that while cool and flavourful, entitlements are difficult to get into and do not give sufficient benefits to make it worth while.<br /> <br /> I find it sad but true. Then the idea got into my head, what needs changing, so I started brainstorming and came to this conclusion: Every Entitlement needs 1) a Token that represents an emblem of the order, and 2) Privileges that offer mechanical benefits that are unlikely to be received through simple pledge or token. I came to this conclusion when I found out that \u201cprivilege\u201d means \u201cprivate law\u201d as such, it should feel that way, private benefits that only entitlement members should have access to. As far as the Emblem Tokens go, these belong to the entitlement holder, other people can't use them, and they won't stray far from the entitlement itself. <br /> <br /> <b>Margravate of the Brim</b><br /> <i>Emblem:</i> Home Field headband<br /> <i>Description:</i> A stained Headband that seems to be covered in the stains of work and toil but never seems to get dirty. It appears to be made of paraphernalia of the local sports team, often manifesting as a sports cap or bandana. <br /> <i>Effect:</i> Every place has advantages, its secrets, and its routines. By activating this token the Margrave can know a place like a local for a scene, the Margrave gains +2 to Investigation and Streetwise rolls to take advantage of this local knowledge.<br /> <i>Catch:</i> The user is helping people who are identified as not belonging to the neighbourhood/area that the Margrave is in.<br /> <i>Drawback:</i> The Margrave is a local now, unless she spends a minimum of four hours in the area\u2019s community after activating this token she will take -1 to all rolls for the rest of the day. <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Safety of the Brim:</i> Increase bonuses to +3<br /> <br /> <i>The Land Takes Care of Its Own:</i> So long as the Margrave remains within the boundaries of her bordermarch, she does not have to worry about the essentials. Her stomach is never empty, her car doesn\u2019t seem to ever need gas, and she is never want for shelter. The Margrave\u2019s resource merit never drops below 1 so long as she is in her bordermarch.<br /> <br /> <i>You\u2019re Not Welcome Here:</i> By identifying threats to her bordermarch and spending a glamour per person, the Margrave penalizes Initiative, Perception, and Stealth by an amount equal to her Wyrd so long as they remain within her bordermarch. <br /> <br /> <b>Scarecrow Ministry: </b><br /> <i>Emblem:</i> Bugbear mask (As Is)<br /> <br /> <i>Quick Work for the Quick:</i> Whenever the Scarecrow Ministry must build one of their sites of horror, the minister may spend a glamour to double the speed by which they construct it per dot of glamour spent for the scene. The Effect of this privilege will be dispelled should anyone but a Scarecrow Minister witness the efforts. This privilege stacks with the Merit :Brownie\u2019s Boon.<br /> <i>Scarecrafter:</i> Ministers receive a +2 bonus to Craft, Expression, and Intimidate to scare people or create things to scare people.<br /> <i>Deep Fear:</i> Ministers receive 2 additional points of glamour instead of one when harvesting their court emotion. <br /> <br /> <b>The Tolltaker Knighthood</b><br /> <i>Emblem:</i> Bounty Badge<br /> <i>Effect:</i> Bounty\u2019s Curse under \u201cTolltaker Knighthood\u201d in the CtL book, ignore the willpower cost.<br /> <i>Catch:</i> The Bounty is wanted locally by a legitimate political body.<br /> <i>Drawback:</i> \u201cYou can Run, but I can\u2019t hide\u201d, when using this Token Emblem the knight is more noticeable to their quarry. The Quarry gains a +2 bonus to spot the knight if the knight is actively trying to conceal themselves from their quarry.<br /> <br /> <i>To the letter:</i> A tolltaker knight cannot accidentally kill someone when performing their duties. If a character is sufficiently wounded that additional damage might kill them, the tolltaker can instead upgrade a single box of damage on the leftmost health box to hurt their target without risking the target\u2019s life and causing the rest to roll over. In the event that any form of additional harm will kill their quarry, the knight will instead apply an appropriate penalty of -3 that will affect the target until they have healed their size in damage. <br /> <i>Brutal Finesse:</i> When using called shot rules to aim for arms and legs the penalty is -1<br /> <i>Rough and Tumble:</i> Knights heal bashing damage at double the speed. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox","name":"danparadox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1838_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-19T08:27:30-07:00","id":202159,"title":"","content":"Hello,<br /> <br /> These are pretty cool. I noticed a similar issue when I ran changeling - most of the entitlement saren't super appealing.<br /> <br /> I like the Magistrates of the wax mask, butI found it odd that their token wasn't a wax mask! Though I guess the &quot;waxen violet&quot; could just be called a wax mask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2734-atwannabe","name":"ATwannabe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2734_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-20T09:39:43-07:00","id":203030,"title":"","content":"These do look cool, but depending on the group it might get abused. In my games I usually just tell the players that if they want an entitlement, they can roleplay getting in and we'll work on priveleges together. That way I don't have to rewrite all of them.<br /> <br /> I also usually let the characters recover willpower by acting &quot;in character&quot; for their entitlement. For example, I had a Pearl Satrap, and he regained a point each time he made a deal, and a Magus of the Gilded Thorn regained one each time she spent time studying something exceptional she found in the hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3316-cantshutup","name":"cantshutup","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-28T20:55:09-07:00","id":212019,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the willpower refill, but what about a glamour refill? You do your duties and the wyrd supplies dividends. <br /> What often gets me about entitlements is the fact that TF's are called &quot;the gentry&quot; which is also the nickname for the landed and titled aristocrats. Obviously most entitlements are about as fond of TF's as they would be towards the bubonic plague, but what about becoming titled makes changeling more like &quot;the gentry&quot; rather than TF's?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1838-danparadox","name":"danparadox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1838_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}